course: dictionary
lesson: 11341
title: Zebra: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A zebra is a wild African animal like a horse, with black and white stripes. The word can also mean something you see on a road. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «Each year more than a million wildebeest, with zebras and gazelles, follow the rain and fresh grass.» The clues are wildebeest, gazelles, rain and grass. These are all about animals and nature, so zebras must be animals here.
explain: Now try a road sentence: «Cross at the zebra, then look both ways and wait for cars to stop.» Cars and waiting to cross tell you the word means a place on the road. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A zebra is a wild African animal like a horse, with black and white stripes.
fact: A zebra has 4 legs.
fact: Zebras eat grass and live in herds on the African plains.
fact: Under its fur, a zebra's skin is black, and every zebra's pattern is unique.
fact: A zebra crossing (UK) is a place on a road with black and white stripes where people can cross.
exercise: «Each year more than a million wildebeest, with zebras and gazelles, follow the rain and fresh grass.» What are zebras in this sentence? | A kind of rain | A sort of fresh grass | *Wild animals that eat grass | A road for cars
exercise: How many legs does a zebra have? | 8 | 2 | *4 | 6
exercise: «Cross at the zebra, then look both ways and wait for cars to stop.» What is the zebra in this sentence? | A sort of car | *A place with black and white stripes where people can cross | A horse that runs very fast | A wild African animal with stripes
test: Under its fur, a zebra's skin is what colour? | Brown | *Black | White | Grey
test: Scientists say every zebra's stripe pattern is what? | Changed by the weather | The same as all the others | *Unique | Painted on each morning
exam: «The quagga, a zebra striped only at the front, died out in 1883.» What does died out mean? | Got much bigger | Went on holiday | Ran away from the zoo | *Stopped existing, with none left alive
